  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to jump up; to spring up; to leap into the air",
      "explanation": "To move upward suddenly by jumping, often from surprise, joy, or excitement."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "06345_tobiagaru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{嬉|うれ}しくて{飛|と}び{上|あ}がった。",
      "english": "I jumped up with joy.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06345_tobiagaru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{大|おお}きな{音|おと}に{驚|おどろ}いて{飛|と}び{上|あ}がった。",
      "english": "I jumped up, startled by the loud noise.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06345_tobiagaru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{子供|こども}たちが{飛|と}び{上|あ}がって{喜|よろこ}んだ。",
      "english": "The children jumped up and down with delight.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive). Compound verb: {飛|と}ぶ + {上|あ}がる.\n\nNUANCE: Often used to express emotional reactions like surprise or joy, rather than deliberate physical movement.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・{喜|よろこ}びで{飛|と}び{上|あ}がる: to jump for joy\n・{驚|おどろ}いて{飛|と}び{上|あ}がる: to jump up in surprise\n・{飛|と}び{上|あ}がって{喜|よろこ}ぶ: to be overjoyed (jumping with happiness)\n\nIDIOMATIC:\n・{飛|と}び{上|あ}がるほど{嬉|うれ}しい: so happy one could jump for joy",
